---
import Term from "../Term.astro";
import Try from "../Try.astro";
import "../sternzeit/sternzeit.css";
import "./dunstkreis.css";
import "./exposureday.css";
---

<figure class="strip-figure exposureday" id="exposure-day">
    <div class="strip-panel exposureday-panel">
        <svg aria-label="The exposure over the chosen day: the light meter's reading, the ramp's compensation and the exposure held in its range"></svg>
        <button type="button" class="view-toggle exposureday-reset" data-field="reset" hidden>reset the ramp</button>
    </div>
    <figcaption class="figure-caption">
        The exposure over the chosen day at the chosen place, in EV<sub>100</sub>, midnight to midnight on the chosen
        clock: what the light meter reads (gray), the reading with the ramp's compensation (dashed), and the exposure
        the sky pass takes (the accent), held at its floor of EV 4. Under it, the ramp's compensation over the day, 0 as
        metered and +1 twice as bright, and the Sun's altitude: day, the golden and the blue hour, then nautical and
        astronomical <Term of="Twilight">twilight</Term>, each a shade darker, and night. At the bottom the ramp itself
        by the Sun's altitude, solid for the rising Sun and dashed for the setting one: drag its keys, hollow where the
        setting Sun has one of its own, and the day above follows. This changes this figure only.
        <Try label="Tromsø at midsummer" set="date=2026-06-21T22:00:00Z&lat=69.65&lon=18.96&h=1" fig="exposure-day">
            the Sun never sets, the exposure about EV 13 at midnight and 16 at noon.
        </Try>
    </figcaption>
</figure>

<script>
    import "./exposureday";
</script>
